WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.089 --> 00:00:05.020
Speaker 1: Throughout this week, we've been
talking qualitatively about the feeling that

00:00:05.020 --> 00:00:07.580
Joe Biden's presidency has turned around.

00:00:07.580 --> 00:00:11.840
We've listed the different accomplishments
over the last two, three months and particularly

00:00:11.840 --> 00:00:13.830
over the last 3 to 4 weeks.

00:00:13.830 --> 00:00:19.060
But we didn't yet have anything quantitative
to answer the question, is there really a

00:00:19.060 --> 00:00:20.270
turnaround happening?

00:00:20.270 --> 00:00:22.720
Is Joe Biden's approval actually increasing?

00:00:22.720 --> 00:00:27.160
And the reason we care about that is not so
much as a curiosity, although it's interesting

00:00:27.160 --> 00:00:31.210
to see a president have such a low approval
rating for a while and then see it recover

00:00:31.210 --> 00:00:39.030
because it's what tends to happen during presidencies
is there's an erosion of approval over time.

00:00:39.030 --> 00:00:43.280
What is interesting about it is its impact
on the November midterms, which are now just

00:00:43.280 --> 00:00:48.660
roughly nine weeks or so away by very, very
rough estimate.

00:00:48.660 --> 00:00:55.450
Looking at the calendar, if indeed Joe Biden's
approval rating continues to increase at the

00:00:55.450 --> 00:01:01.329
rate at which it has over the last ten days,
it is all of a sudden looking very bad for

00:01:01.329 --> 00:01:03.120
Republicans in November.

00:01:03.120 --> 00:01:05.289
So the first question is, what are the numbers?

00:01:05.289 --> 00:01:11.130
Well, Joe Biden's approval rating has spiked
11% in a very short period of time.

00:01:11.130 --> 00:01:19.649
Now, for those who may or may not understand
the precision with which I am speaking, 11%

00:01:19.649 --> 00:01:23.639
increase is not an 11 point increase.

00:01:23.639 --> 00:01:31.919
The approval rating of Joe Biden bottomed
out at 37 and a half right on July 21st.

00:01:31.919 --> 00:01:35.829
And it has now gone up to 41.6%.

00:01:35.829 --> 00:01:43.399
That is, of course, not an increase of 11
percentage points, but it is an 11% increase

00:01:43.399 --> 00:01:44.840
in one month.

00:01:44.840 --> 00:01:46.399
That is significant.

00:01:46.399 --> 00:01:53.229
And if you see even half or two thirds of
that increase continue until November, you're

00:01:53.229 --> 00:01:59.869
going to have a quite popular Joe Biden on
the day of the midterm elections, because

00:01:59.869 --> 00:02:06.259
these midterms are, in a sense, referenda
on those in power, which in this case includes

00:02:06.259 --> 00:02:10.799
a Democrat in the White House, Democrats controlling
the Senate, although barely, and Democrats

00:02:10.799 --> 00:02:12.129
controlling the House.

00:02:12.129 --> 00:02:15.959
The conventional wisdom would be that would
be very good for Democrats.

00:02:15.959 --> 00:02:19.480
And you can tell that Biden is sort of reinvigorated
in a sense.

00:02:19.480 --> 00:02:26.180
He is back on the campaign trail and starting
to be visibly campaigning for Democrats running

00:02:26.180 --> 00:02:27.180
in November.

00:02:27.180 --> 00:02:36.170
Yesterday, at a rally against a Trump allied
Republican in Maryland, he gave a quite good

00:02:36.170 --> 00:02:40.920
speech in which he slammed the MAGA movement
as semi fascism.

00:02:40.920 --> 00:02:42.359
And I think that that's a pretty good term.

00:02:42.359 --> 00:02:52.780
I sometimes call it wannabe fascism, wet dream,
fascism, authoritarian, you know, wishing

00:02:52.780 --> 00:02:54.200
whatever you want to call it.

00:02:54.200 --> 00:02:56.420
Joe Biden, back out there.

00:02:56.420 --> 00:02:58.810
And listen, these are just empirical questions.

00:02:58.810 --> 00:03:01.430
There was the feeling that there was a turnaround.

00:03:01.430 --> 00:03:03.769
That turnaround is very much reflected.

00:03:03.769 --> 00:03:04.769
This is.

00:03:04.769 --> 00:03:07.109
And by the way, if you look.

00:03:07.109 --> 00:03:13.329
Even though the number is still under 42%
for Biden's approval, the rate at which it

00:03:13.329 --> 00:03:19.930
increased is significant, and we have not
seen that during Biden's presidency so far.

00:03:19.930 --> 00:03:25.510
It matches essentially the quickest decline
that we saw in August of 2021 as Republicans

00:03:25.510 --> 00:03:30.319
were slamming Biden for the pullout from Afghanistan
and Colbert numbers were not looking good.

00:03:30.319 --> 00:03:35.280
This is as rapid an increase as we have seen
a decrease during the Biden presidency, and

00:03:35.280 --> 00:03:36.799
we still have time.

00:03:36.799 --> 00:03:38.799
But it so far bodes very, very well

